#
# /etc/pam.d/kde-smartcard — third, non-interactive PAM conversation of the
# screen locker (KSCREENLOCKER_PAM_SMARTCARD_SERVICE): inserting a
# registered smart card unlocks. Like kde-fingerprint it must not ask for a
# password. Skipped silently unless libpam-pkcs11 is installed and
# configured (/etc/pam_pkcs11/); pam_deny then ends the conversation.
-auth   [success=done authinfo_unavail=die default=bad]   pam_pkcs11.so wait_for_card card_only
auth    required                                          pam_deny.so
